{
  "name": "Howland Current Pump (V→I Converter)",
  "description": "A Howland voltage-controlled current source: an op-amp with matched positive/negative feedback resistors forces a load current proportional to the input voltage and independent of the load resistance. Sweep or step the load — the current stays constant (≈0.099mA/V, <0.2% change across a 2:1 load swing) while the load voltage scales. (Validated on ngspice.)",
